"""Build an auditable subsystem backport plan between two kernel histories.

Unlike a path-only missing-commit finder, this tool:
  * identifies downstream backports by exact SHA, embedded upstream SHA, and
    stable patch-id;
  * starts from commits touching a requested subsystem/path set;
  * expands the set with explicit Fixes relationships, hunk-context provenance,
    and definitions of newly-used symbols that were introduced outside the
    subsystem or before the requested planning base;
  * can dry-run the resulting series in a temporary worktree and use conflicts
    to discover additional context commits;
  * flags later upstream merge resolutions touching candidate files.

It is intentionally conservative: subject equality is reported as a hint, never
accepted as proof that a commit is already downstream.
"""

